"html": "<p>Cosmic Measurements of the Great Pyramid of Giza: The 138 Protocol</p>\n<p>Second Edition, Expanded &amp; Revised — Consolidated Master Text</p>\n<p>© 2026 Bradley Rogue / Hollywood Rogue Ventures LLC</p>\n<p>Phoenix Chronicles Universe • youtube.com/@PhoenixChroniclesUniverse</p>\n<p>All measurements cited in this work derive from Sir Flinders Petrie, <em>The Pyramids and Temples of Gizeh</em> (London: Field &amp; Tuer, 1883). The interpretive framework is based on the Archaix research of Jason Breshears (Archaix.com) and his book <em>Chronicon</em> (2017).</p>\n<p>Bradley Rogue is a researcher, author, and former Nashville Editor in Chief of <em>Cash Box Magazine</em>. His pyramid research is the 138 experience: thirty-eight years (1988–2026, twice nineteen), begun on 1/19 — the one and the thirty-eight that spell its name — across three continents and three visits to the Giza plateau — with a fourth, a solo return, planned for March 2027. He has also climbed into the echo chamber atop El Castillo at Chichén Itzá, and heard the stone answer back.</p>\n<p>All rights reserved.</p>\n<p>First publication of this edition: March 10, 2026 — Day 69 of the year • 12,834 days from January 19, 1991 • 138 × 93</p>\n<p>Revised: June 3, 2026 — 6 + 3 + 2 + 0 + 2 + 6 = 19</p>\n<p>Consolidated: June 5, 2026 — Day 156 of the year, and 156 = 12 × 13: the digit sum of 138 multiplied by its first two digits. From January 19, 1991, to this consolidation is exactly 12,921 days — and 1-2-9-2-1 reads the same forward and backward. The master text closes on a palindrome.</p>"
