"html": "<p><em>“<strong>These are the tools that are necessary to determine the precision on the artifacts. These are modern tools. These tools do not exist in the archaeological record.</strong>”</em></p>\n<p>— Christopher Dunn</p>\n<p><em>“<strong>I tried many shapes, many heights, but eventually I returned to what is called the proportion of the Egyptian.</strong>”</em></p>\n<p>— I.M. Pei</p>\n<p><strong>“Any serious researcher of The Great Pyramid of Giza would do well to study the measurements with Petrie, then measure the time with Breshears…”</strong></p>\n<p>— Bradley Rogue</p>\n<h3>“Real Eyes Realize Real Lies.”</h3>\n<p>— Ancient Wisdom</p>\n<h3>“All of this was accomplished with copper tools, ropes and slaves, in just 20 years, during the reign of Khufu, while the rest of the world’s inhabitants were simply nomads clad in animal skins…”</h3>\n<p>— Modern Egyptology</p>\n<h3>“We were techno-lithic, and ancient, and we have something to say, an unspoken secret of sorts…”</h3>\n<p>— The Builders of The Great Pyramid of Giza</p>"
