"html": "<h3>142 Through 199 · Above the Protocol</h3>\n<p>The master closed upon 138, the protocol — and there it set down its minus sign. Sixty-three courses of the lower cycle, 35 through 97, fell below that climb and could not keep their places among numbered leaves; they are remembered in the essays that follow, not counted here. Above the protocol the count simply goes on, and each page is once more its own number: <strong>138 + 4 = 142</strong>, and onward, page after page, climbing toward 199 — the mirror prime. The minus has become a plus. The descent was always an ascent.</p>"
